            "text": "I've proposed one entry and one connection from your highlight, for you to accept or reject.\n\n**Dimension: political.** The passage is about who controlled the money. Athens moved the treasury perhaps \"as a pretext to gain control of the League's finances\". Taking control of the allies' funds is a question of power, not of wealth itself.\n\n**New entry: \"Treasury of the Delian League moved to Athens\", 454–453 BCE.** It's set as a span in Athens under Politics & government. Neither your Chronicle nor the linked pages already have it. Delos is marked as a place, so it can only appear in the entry's wording, not as a connection end.\n\n**Connection: the transfer weakened the Delian League (your existing entry).** It put the League's money under Athens's control.\n\n**What I left out:**\n- **The causes the passage gives:** the defeat in Egypt and the allies' revolts. Neither has a date in this section, so I didn't make entries for them. Without entries, they can't be linked to the transfer.\n- **Pericles:** I didn't connect him. The passage says \"Athens\" moved the treasury, not him."
